==Strategy==
These first ten stages are designed to showcase Big Peng Z as an enemy and can easily be solved with brute force. Focus on killing the Scissoroos and chipping down Big Peng Z and you should be able to secure a relatively easy win.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]]: With a very consistent anti-Alien/Zombie Curse ability at midrange, Fried Chicken Cat's LD can easily connect onto Big Peng Z and disable his Toxic ability, even behind other threats, trivializing the stage as long as other units are brought along to defeat the nasty peons.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Seafarer's decent generalist stats and 40% Freeze ability versus Aliens allows him to easily shut down the Aliens, as he can outrange them reliably.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Housewife's strong LD ability and Zombie Killer, combined with her damage if a Savage Blow hits makes her essential here, since Big Peng Z's low standing range of 150 often causes him to walk into her range, where her Slow ability, if it activates, can greatly impede him.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: If you're really struggling here, you can use Cyberpunk to Slow the boss and all of the enemies, allowing you to take your time while you chip the boss down.
*[[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]]: Completely destroys this stage, being able to tank huge amounts of damage from Big Peng Z and having the Curse ability against Big Peng Z as well as having decent generalist stats. Brainwashed Island is best sent out after most of the peons are gone.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any unit with Toxic Immune, Curse vs. Zombies, or both will alleviate the stage's difficulty as long as they can deny Big Peng Z's Toxic ability. Examples include [[Mighty Carrowsell (Uber Rare Cat)|Extradimensional Envanz]] and [[Bliza (Uber Rare Cat)|Blizarena]].
